===2016 onwards===
In July 2015 it was announced that the [[Independent Foreign Fiction Prize|''Independent'' Foreign Fiction Prize]] would be disbanded and its prize money would be folded into the Man Booker International Prize.<ref name=shaffi/> Starting with the 2016 award, the Man Booker International Prize became annual and changed its remit to perform the same role as the ''Independent'' prize: awarding books of fiction translated into English, in order to encourage the publishing and reading of quality works in translation and to highlight the work of translators.<ref name=orthofer>{{cite web |url=http://www.complete-review.com/saloon/archive/201507a.htm#rv1 |title=Man Booker Independent International Foreign Fiction Prize |work=[[complete review]] |author=Michael Orthofer |date=8 July 2015 |access-date=8 July 2015 |archive-date=28 February 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210228093759/https://www.complete-review.com/saloon/archive/201507a.htm#rv1 |url-status=live }}</ref> The £50,000 prize is split between author and translator. Each shortlisted author and translator receives £2,500.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The International Booker Prize and its History |url=https://thebookerprizes.com/the-international-booker-prize/the-international-booker-prize-and-its-history |access-date=2023-04-17 |website=The Booker Prizes |language=en |archive-date=16 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220816124421/https://thebookerprizes.com/the-international-booker-prize/the-international-booker-prize-and-its-history |url-status=live }}</ref> Judges select a longlist of 12 or 13 books in March ("the Booker Dozen"), followed by a shortlist of six in April,<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://thebookerprizes.com/sites/default/files/2022-08/220815%20Booker%20International%202023%20Rules.pdf|title=Full rules for the international Booker prize, in PDF format|access-date=17 April 2023|archive-date=20 June 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230620101724/https://thebookerprizes.com/sites/default/files/2022-08/220815%20Booker%20International%202023%20Rules.pdf|url-status=live}}</ref> with the winner announced in May.<ref>{{cite web|title=Evolution of the Man Booker International Prize announced |url=http://themanbookerprize.com/resources/media/pressreleases/2015/07/07/evolution-man-booker-international-prize-announced|website=The Man Booker Prizes|access-date=18 May 2016|archive-date=4 June 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160604033140/http://themanbookerprize.com/resources/media/pressreleases/2015/07/07/evolution-man-booker-international-prize-announced|url-status=dead}}</ref> 

In July 2026, it was announced that [[Dmitry Bukhman#Philanthropy|Bukhman Philanthropies]] would sponsor the prize for the next 10 years. The prize was renamed the Bukhman International Booker Prize, and the winning prize was increased from £50,000 to £100,000. The shortlist prize remained the same.<ref>{{cite web |title=Bukhman Philanthropies to fund next decade of the International Booker Prize as judges announced for the 2027 prize {{!}} The Booker Prizes |url=https://thebookerprizes.com/media-centre/press-releases/bukhman-philanthropies-fund-next-decade-of-the-international-booker-prize |website=Booker Prizes |access-date=2 July 2026 |language=en |date=2 July 2026}}</ref> 

