===2018===
The longlist for the ninth Man Booker International Prize was announced on 12 March 2018. The shortlist of six books was announced on 12 April 2018 at an event at Somerset House in London. The winner was announced on 22 May 2018 at the Victoria & Albert Museum in London. Olga Tokarczuk is the first [[Literature in Poland|Polish author]] to win the award,<ref>{{cite news|title=Man Booker International Prize: Olga Tokarczuk is first Polish winner|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-44219438|date=22 May 2018|access-date=24 May 2018|agency=BBC News|archive-date=28 October 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211028183049/https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-44219438|url-status=live}}</ref> and shared the prize with translator Jennifer Croft.<ref>{{cite news|title=Polish novelist Olga Tokarczuk wins Man Booker International Prize for translated novel 'Flights'|url=http://www.dw.com/en/polish-novelist-olga-tokarczuk-wins-man-booker-international-prize-for-translated-novel-flights/a-43887975|date=May 22, 2018|access-date=25 May 2018|agency=DW.com|archive-date=24 May 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180524223001/http://www.dw.com/en/polish-novelist-olga-tokarczuk-wins-man-booker-international-prize-for-translated-novel-flights/a-43887975|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Lisa Appignanesi]] described Tokarczuk as a "writer of wonderful wit, imagination, and literary panache."<ref>{{cite news|title=Olga Tokarczuk becomes first Polish winner of International Man Booker Prize|url=https://home.bt.com/news/showbiz-news/olga-tokarczuk-becomes-first-polish-winner-of-international-man-booker-prize-11364273590189|access-date=22 May 2018|publisher=BT|date=22 May 2018|archive-date=23 May 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180523100832/https://home.bt.com/news/showbiz-news/olga-tokarczuk-becomes-first-polish-winner-of-international-man-booker-prize-11364273590189|url-status=live}}</ref>

