===2026===
The longlist was announced on 24 February 2026<ref>{{Cite web |title=The International Booker Prize 2026 |url=https://thebookerprizes.com/the-booker-library/prize-years/international/2026 |access-date=2026-02-24 |website=The Booker Prizes |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Creamer |first=Ella |date=2026-02-24 |title=Witches, Nazi collaborators and banned books: International Booker prize announces 2026 longlist |url=https://www.theguardian.com/books/2026/feb/24/ravn-kehlmann-genberg-enard-and-cabezon-camara-longlist-international-booker-prize |access-date=2026-02-24 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref> and the shortlist on 31 March 2026.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Marshall |first1=Alex |title=International Booker Prize Shortlist: 6 Novels With 'Burning Humanity' |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/31/books/international-booker-prize-shortlist.html |work=The New York Times |date=31 March 2026}}</ref> The winner, Yáng Shuāng-zǐ's ''[[Taiwan Travelogue]]'', was announced on 19 May 2026 at the [[Tate Modern]] in London.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The International Booker Prize 2026 |url=https://thebookerprizes.com/the-booker-library/prize-years/international/2026 |access-date=2026-02-27 |website=The Booker Prizes |language=en}}</ref> ''Taiwan Travelogue'' is the first book written in Mandarin and the first book by a Taiwanese author to win.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Marshall |first1=Alex |title=International Booker Prize 2026: 'Taiwan Travelogue' is First Winner Originally Written in Mandarin |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/19/books/international-booker-prize-taiwan-travelogue.html |access-date=19 May 2026 |work=The New York Times |date=19 May 2026}}</ref> The judging panel was chaired by British writer [[Natasha Brown (author)|Natasha Brown]] alongside Oxford professor and mathematician [[Marcus du Sautoy]], International Booker Prize-shortlisted translator [[Sophie Hughes]], Kenyan writer and editor [[Troy Onyango]], and Indian novelist and columnist [[Nilanjana Roy]]. 

In 2026, ''The Vegetarian'' was voted the readers' favourite of all the Booker winners in the last ten years.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-05-11|title="The Vegetarian" voted most popular International Booker Prize winner|url=https://www.booksandpublishing.com.au/articles/2026/05/11/329348/the-vegetarian-voted-most-popular-international-booker-prize-winner/|access-date=2026-05-12|publisher=Books+Publishing}}</ref> 
